/Title (Final defence: the intentionally defective block policy is unsuitable for the ordered unequal-cost workload because it concentrates expensive tasks in one worker. Round-robin and dynamic assignment are credible alternatives with different overheads. The best choice must be based on task-conservation checks and repeated measurements, not on an assumed universal winner.)
